a file system,

00:08:48.110 --> 00:08:50.750
it is not traditional
like a traditional file

00:08:50.750 --> 00:08:53.630
system that can be accessed
by applications and users.

00:08:53.630 --> 00:08:55.730
The file system is
essentially locked down

00:08:55.730 --> 00:08:58.190
and is not
accessible, and is not

00:08:58.190 --> 00:08:59.580
accessible by the application.

00:08:59.580 --> 00:09:01.550
So it really reduces
the attack vector

00:09:01.550 --> 00:09:05.190
that malicious applications
would have on the device.

00:09:05.190 --> 00:09:08.130
Additionally, by reducing the
actual data-- the user data

00:09:08.130 --> 00:09:11.330
and your company data-- on the
device, if the device is lost,

00:09:11.330 --> 00:09:14.000
you can be assured that company
data isn't on the device,

00:09:14.000 --> 00:09:15.890
because the data's
used in the cloud

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:18.410
and is not stored
locally on the device.

00:09:18.410 --> 00:09:25.340
But we can also know that if the
data is stored on the device,

00:09:25.340 --> 00:09:28.100
it is in an encrypted partition,
and they use a partition.

00:09:28.100 --> 00:09:30.510
And finally, a feature that's
very popular in Chrome OS

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:32.180
is what's called
ephemeral mode, which

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:34.610
means every time the user
enters and exits their session,

00:09:34.610 --> 00:09:38.160
any local data, any cached
data is wiped every single time

00:09:38.160 --> 00:09:40.040
so they have a
clean user session,

00:09:40.040 --> 00:09:41.480
and no data is left behind.

00:09:41.480 --> 00:09:42.925
There's no data footprint.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:47.430
So regularly
